# `structure::MotionState`

The initial displacement and velocity of a time integration.

## Signature

```cpp
structure::MotionState
```

## What It Does

The starting state of `motion`. Either field may be left undefined, and an undefined field means zero.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `displacement` | Initial node displacements, `[..., node, 3]`. | undefined (zero) |
| `velocity` | Initial node velocities, `[..., node, 3]`. | undefined (zero) |

## Returns

A value; validated by `motion`.

## Errors

Shapes, dtype or platform different from the frame, or a non-zero value at a supported degree of freedom, are rejected by `motion`.

## Interpretation and Use

Start from a mode shape to excite one mode, from a static deflection to release a loaded structure, or from a rigid rotation to start a swing. Omitting the state starts the structure at rest in its undeformed configuration.

